("England", "Digital subscription renewal", "An annual software subscription renewed yesterday at twice the previous price. I received an email three days beforehand and had trouble finding cancellation. I live in England and use it personally. What terms, dates and current law should be checked?"),
("England", "Lost parcel risk", "A retailer's courier left my order outside my door without my permission, and it disappeared. The retailer says delivery tracking ends its responsibility. I did not nominate a neighbour or safe place. What should I do?"),
("England", "Small claim limitation", "A contractor did poor work at my home several years ago. I know the completion date but discovered concealed defects later. Before deciding if I am out of time, what facts about contract, damage, concealment and dates do you need?"),
("England", "Witnessing a will", "My parent signed a paper will at home while two friends watched by video call this week. Nobody was physically in the room. Is that enough under the law currently in force? Do not assume pandemic temporary rules still apply."),
("England", "Online defamation", "Someone publicly posted that my café falsifies food-safety records. I say this is false, but I cannot yet quantify lost customers. What issues determine whether a defamation claim is realistic and what should I preserve?"),
("California, USA", "Security deposit return", "I moved out of a Los Angeles apartment 30 days ago. The landlord kept my $2,000 deposit and sent no itemised statement. I rented the whole apartment and have move-out photographs. What California rules and exceptions should I check?"),
